{
  "id": "en02-presente",
  "title": "El presente y la vida diaria (A1 – A2)",
  "description": "Present simple y continuous, frecuencia, preguntas, can, cantidades, pronombres objeto y vocabulario cotidiano.",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "l01-present-simple",
      "title": "Present simple: hábitos y hechos",
      "summary": "Cómo se forma, la s de la tercera persona y los auxiliares do y does.",
      "minutes": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "concepto",
          "text": "El **present simple** se usa para lo que es **siempre o habitualmente** así: rutinas («I study every day»), hechos («Water boils at 100 °C») y horarios («The class starts at 7»). En textos de ingeniería es el tiempo más común, porque describe cómo funcionan las cosas.",
          "title": "Para qué sirve"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Forma",
            "I / you / we / they",
            "he / she / it"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Afirmativa",
              "I work",
              "She work**s**"
            ],
            [
              "Negativa",
              "I do not (don't) work",
              "She does not (doesn't) work"
            ],
            [
              "Pregunta",
              "Do you work?",
              "Does she work?"
            ],
            [
              "Respuesta corta",
              "Yes, I do. / No, I don't.",
              "Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "importante",
          "text": "En **afirmativo**, he / she / it llevan **s** en el verbo: «He work**s**». Pero en negativo y pregunta la s se la lleva el auxiliar (**does**) y el verbo vuelve a su forma base: «Does he **work**?», no «Does he works?».",
          "title": "La s solo aparece una vez"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Regla de la tercera persona",
            "Ejemplos"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "General: + s",
              "works, plays, reads"
            ],
            [
              "Termina en s, sh, ch, x, o: + es",
              "watches, goes, does, fixes"
            ],
            [
              "Consonante + y: ies",
              "study → studies; carry → carries"
            ],
            [
              "Irregular",
              "have → has"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "concepto",
          "text": "**Do / does** son verbos «ayudantes»: no se traducen; solo sirven para armar la negación y la pregunta. Piensa en ellos como el signo «¿» del inglés.",
          "title": "El auxiliar"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Inglés",
            "Español"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "I study civil engineering.",
              "Estudio ingeniería civil."
            ],
            [
              "She lives in Cuenca.",
              "Ella vive en Cuenca."
            ],
            [
              "We don't have class on Saturdays.",
              "No tenemos clase los sábados."
            ],
            [
              "Does he speak English? — Yes, he does.",
              "¿Él habla inglés? — Sí."
            ],
            [
              "Steel expands when it is heated.",
              "El acero se dilata cuando se calienta."
            ],
            [
              "The river flows from north to south.",
              "El río fluye de norte a sur."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Completa: «She (…) in a construction company.»",
          "options": [
            "work",
            "works",
            "working",
            "is work"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "Tercera persona + s."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Completa: «(…) he study at night?»",
          "options": [
            "Do",
            "Does",
            "Is",
            "Are"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "He → does."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "La negación correcta:",
          "options": [
            "He don't work",
            "He doesn't works",
            "He doesn't work",
            "He not works"
          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "Doesn't + verbo base."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "La tercera persona de «study» es:",
          "options": [
            "studys",
            "studies",
            "studyes",
            "study"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "y → ies."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "El present simple se usa para:",
          "options": [
            "Acciones en este momento",
            "Hábitos y hechos",
            "El pasado",
            "Planes ya decididos"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "Rutinas y verdades generales."
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Completa: «They (…) coffee.» (negativo)",
          "options": [
            "doesn't drink",
            "don't drink",
            "aren't drink",
            "not drink"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "They → don't."
        }
      ]
    },
